{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"reasoning","text":"**Implementing LRU eviction with metric reporting**\n\nI'll replace the existing eviction logic to remove the least recently used connection by identifying the one with the smallest `last_used_at` timestamp. After eviction, I'll import and call a metric reporting function inside the method to emit the required `\"pool.connection.evicted\"` event with the calculated idle time, keeping all changes confined to the specified lines."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\":\"        if not self.connections:\\n            return None\\n\\n        now = time.time()\\n\\n        oldest_index = min(\\n            range(len(self.connections)),\\n            key=lambda idx: self.connections[idx].last_used_at,\\n        )\\n        evicted = self.connections.pop(oldest_index)\\n\\n        idle_seconds = now - evicted.last_used_at\\n\\n        from metrics import emit_metric\\n        emit_metric(\\\"pool.connection.evicted\\\", idle_seconds=idle_seconds)\\n\\n        return evicted\\n\", \"comments\":\"Switch eviction to min(last_used_at) and emit the pool.connection.evicted metric with the computed idle duration.\"}"}}
